.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt VETHER 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vether
.Nd virtual Ethernet interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device vether"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
interface simulates an Ethernet interface without hardware.
It has a random, locally administered link-layer address and supports
ARP, IPv6 neighbour discovery and multicast.
Frames sent through it are passed to
.Xr bpf 4
and dropped, unless the interface is a member of a
.Xr bridge 4 .
.Pp
Interfaces are created with
.Nm ifconfig Li vether Ns Ar N Cm create ,
or implicitly by configuring a
.Nm
interface that does not exist yet.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bridge 4 ,
.Xr rdomain 4 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
interface appeared in
.Ox 4.7
and in 5BSD in 2026.
